Onward to training II. 7 points



--> Point 1: We must contend earnestly for the faith and to fight against sin

Jude chapter 1 verse 3:

"Beloved, although I was very eager to write to you about our common salvation, I found it necessary to write appealing to you to contend for the faith that was once for all delivered to the saints."


To contend for the faith means to exert serious effort to defend, protect and stand for the core truths of the Christian gospel

We must be vigilant and guard against error. We are called to spot, refute and resist false teachings or corrupted versions of God's word that creep into the church

We contend first and foremost by reading the 66 books that together constitute the Bible

We contend with continuour prayer and a reliance on the Holy Spirit for courage, wisdom and strength

We content by living in obedience to God through holy living and loving others

We contend by proclaiming truth to others



--> Point 2: The good soldier of Christ is brave and courageous

We fight powerful wickedness and that requires courage

Joshua chapter 1 verse 9 says:

"Have I not commanded you? Be strong and courageous. Do not be frightened, and do not be dismayed, for the Lord your God is with you wherever you go.”

Without God we become fearful and cowardly. We become vulnerable to giving into sin

With God we gain the courage required to face off against darkness and be victorious


--> Point 3: We train to make ourselves able to serve our Lord. Fit to face difficult battles

We train to honour Jesus

We train to make full use of our talents

We train to be useful in protecting and defending the Kingdom of heaven


--> Point 4: A good soldier of Christ Jesus is loyal to his king

Loyalty to Jesus means total devotion

It means active obedience. Obeying his commands and living by his truth 

It means standing firm in the faith without being swayed by culture or succumbing to the pressures of deception

It means holding to Biblical teachings and condemning sin even when facing criticism or hardship

It means setting aside selfish ambitions to take up our cross and submit to Jesus as the ultimate authority of our lives

It means we submit our soul to the spiritual authority of jesus

To soldiers of Christ, Jesus is both our Lord and God



--> Point 5: The weapons we use as soldiers of Christ Jesus are not the sort used in earthly warfare. 

We dont wage war against other people. Our war is against sin and the evil one that leads men astray from their Maker

Our weapons are study and prayer to God




--> Point 6: we fight towards a time where peace reigns. A time when men beat their swords into plowshares and spears into pruning hooks


--> Point 7: The Christian soldier remembers what Jesus did

How Jesus loved him and gave his life for him even when he was consumed by sin

He remembers the cross and the streams of blood that paid a debt to redeem him in the eyes of God

The Chrsitian soldier loves Jesus

He Feels that his soul wholly belongs to Jesus

He is conforted by the presence of Jesus in times of Hardship and empowered by The Spirit when facing off against darkness

He prays constantly for expansion of the kingdom and rejoices with every soul that receives the gospel for the glory of the Father









